Third-party content vendored into examples/plugin-eval/vendor/
==================================================

The plugins under `examples/plugin-eval/vendor/` are NOT part of 100xtools. They are copies of
third-party work, included so the example eval cases resolve and run from a clean clone
with no network access.

    Source:    https://github.com/anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins
    Path:      {design, engineering}
    Commit:    2cf42948f0b79c5492bb38981752b815fc6788ec
    Date:      2026-08-10
    Copyright: Anthropic, PBC
    Licence:   Apache License 2.0 — see examples/plugin-eval/vendor/LICENSE

    Modifications: NONE. Both plugin directories are byte-for-byte copies of the
    upstream directories at the commit above.

Why they are vendored rather than fetched
-----------------------------------------
An eval case names the plugin it exercises as a path, and a case whose plugin directory is
missing fails to load. Fetching at run time would leave a fresh clone with two broken cases
until a script ran, and would make CI depend on network access to validate them. Pinning a
copy to one commit also makes the examples reproducible: they assert how *this* snapshot
behaves, so a change upstream cannot silently rewrite what the examples claim.

Updating the snapshot
---------------------
Re-copy the two directories from a newer commit, update the commit and date above, and
re-run the example cases. Expect the assertions to need review: they describe how the
plugins actually behave, not how they ought to.

Note for readers
----------------
`examples/plugin-eval/vendor/` is excluded from this repo's own static sweep — vendored third-party code
is not ours to score. Lint it deliberately if you want to:

    python3 plugins/100xeval/skills/100xeval/scripts/run.py \
      eval --static-only --target examples/plugin-eval/vendor/design
